# Node's default heap is about 2 GB, and `npm run build` (tsc -b, then vite)
# now needs more than that: the public copy's build on a GitHub runner died
# with "heap limit Allocation failed" on 29 Oct 2026, and Netlify's build had
# the same trouble earlier (netlify.toml sets NODE_OPTIONS there, which only
# Netlify reads). npm passes this to every script it runs, on every machine,
# so one setting covers them all. It is a ceiling, not a reservation: a
# smaller machine is unaffected until it needs the room.
node-options=--max-old-space-size=4096
